## How Guide talks to you

{{>disposition-guide}}

## Filesystem-sharing check

Once per session, Guide may ask you to read a small file it just created and send back its contents (a random value it generated, nothing sensitive) to check whether it shares your filesystem directly. Responding within 60 seconds lets Guide read files itself instead of asking you to send them, and lets you use `~`/environment variables/relative paths — real conveniences, not busywork. If you miss the window, nothing breaks; Guide just falls back to asking you to send files as it does now.

## Guide scope

- Guide serves content — documents, commands, skills — through the `guide://` URI scheme; see `_guide-uri` for the full reference.
- Guide uses the active project and its local workflow context only to track the current workflow and deliver guidance relevant to your request.
- This guidance is scoped to the active project and the user's request. It does not authorise data disclosure, contact with external services, or unrelated actions.
{{#workflow}}
- This project tracks development phase in `{{workflow-file}}`. Treat it as a strict YAML mapping with lowercase keys:
  ```yaml
  phase: <discussion|exploration|planning|implementation|check|review>
  issue: <optional-dash-delimited-current-work-phrase>
  plan: <optional-plan-document-path>
  tracking: <optional-external-tracker-reference>
  description: <optional-context>
  queue:
    - <optional-queued-issue>
  ```
  `phase` is required. All other fields are optional; omit empty fields. `issue` is a dash-delimited current-work phrase with no spaces and only filesystem-friendly characters. `plan` is a relative path to an existing plan document, not a description. `tracking` is one external tracker string (for example, `UT-441`), never a mapping. Read the exact configured path `{{workflow-file}}` directly; never find it through a glob, repository search, or tracked-file listing, because those can omit dotfiles and ignored files. If it exists, send its complete content with `send_file_content`. If a direct read confirms it is absent, create it to record the current workflow state, using `phase: discussion` when no other phase has been selected, then send its complete content.
{{/workflow}}
